  "analyzed_vuln": {
    "function": "Visit",
    "file": "arrow/cpp/src/arrow/array/validate.cc",
    "description": "In ValidateArrayDataVisitor::Visit(const UnionArray&), union type codes are used as indexes into child_ids (and later child_lengths) with only a negative check. The code does `child_ids[code]` without validating that `code < child_ids.size()` (or <=255 for child_lengths), so malformed IPC data can supply an out-of-range positive type code and trigger an out-of-bounds read (ASan global-buffer-overflow) during RecordBatch::ValidateFull.",
    "conditions": "FuzzIpcStream parses attacker-controlled IPC stream bytes into a RecordBatch containing a UnionArray (seen via nested list validation). During ValidateArrayData, for each non-null union slot, `type_codes[i]` is read from untrusted buffers. If a non-null entry has a positive type code not present in the union type mapping (i.e., beyond child_ids bounds), the validator indexes child_ids/child_lengths out of bounds before returning Invalid, causing the crash."
  },
